# Zell Dincht ({2}{R}, a 0/3): "You may play an additional land on each of your turns", so Bot1 plays two lands on turn 1 (a
# third is refused) and Zell gets +1/+0 for each land Bot1 controls - Bot1's two Mountains, not Bot2's Island and not Zell
# himself: a 2/3. At the beginning of Bot1's end step a land Bot1 chooses returns to its owner's hand (Mountain), leaving
# Zell a 1/3 with one land. On turn 3 Bot1 plays two lands again (Island and Mountain) and Zell is a 3/3.

